{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019mcYwtqKVTEpE5ysjyVqLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*****************************************************************************\n2\t * Copyright (C) 2010 Tadeus Prastowo (eus@member.fsf.org)                   *\n3\t *                                                                           *\n4\t * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify      *\n5\t * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by      *\n6\t * the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or         *\n7\t * (at your option) any later version.                                       *\n8\t *                                                                           *\n9\t * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,           *\n10\t * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of            *\n11\t * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the             *\n12\t * GNU General Public License for more details.                              *\n13\t *                                                                           *\n14\t * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License         *\n15\t * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.     *\n16\t *************************************************************************//**\n17\t * @file razz_simulation.h\n18\t * @brief The Razz simulation engine.\n19\t * @author Tadeus Prastowo <eus@member.fsf.org>\n20\t ****************************************************************************/\n21\t\n22\t#include <stdint.h>\n23\t#include \"card.h\"\n24\t\n25\t#ifndef RAZZ_SIMULATION_H\n26\t#define RAZZ_SIMULATION_H\n27\t\n28\t#ifdef __cplusplus\n29\textern \"C\" {\n30\t#endif\n31\t\n32\t/** The cards that are not played in the simulated game. */\n33\tstruct decided_cards\n34\t{\n35\t  uint8_t my_card_count; /**< The number of my cards. */\n36\t  const card *my_cards[3]; /**< My initial three cards. */\n37\t  uint8_t opponent_card_count; /**< The total number of opponents' cards. */\n38\t  const card *opponent_cards[7]; /**< The initial card of the opponent. */\n39\t};\n40\t\n41\t/**\n42\t * Listens to the final rank of my hand at the end of each game.\n43\t *\n44\t * @param [in] arg your marshalled argument into the listener.\n45\t * @param [in] r the rank of my hand.\n46\t */\n47\ttypedef void (*rank_listener) (void *arg, enum card_rank r);\n48\t\n49\t/**\n50\t * Runs a Razz game for a number of times.\n51\t *\n52\t * @param [in] decided_cards the cards that will not be included in the simulated\n53\t *                           dealing.\n54\t * @param [in] game_count the number of Razz games to be simulated.\n55\t * @param [in] arg your marshalled argument into the listener.\n56\t * @param [in] listener the callback function that will be invoked with the rank\n57\t *                      of my hand at the end of each game.\n58\t *\n59\t * @return 0 if the simulation encounters no error or non-zero if it encounters\n60\t *         one.\n61\t */\n62\tint\n63\tsimulate_razz_game (const struct decided_cards *decided_cards,\n64\t\t\t    unsigned long game_count,\n65\t\t\t    void *arg,\n66\t\t\t    rank_listener listener);\n67\t\n68\t#ifdef __cplusplus\n69\t}\n70\t#endif\n71\t\n72\t#endif /* RAZZ_SIMULATION_H */\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebd4b005-5aaa-4374-8dd0-9b978f6887f6","uuid":"e9261766-5fd7-48bc-951f-bb3473797324","timestamp":"2026-05-28T22:27:38.051Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-0iSo6p/project/c_src/razz_simulation.h","content":"/*****************************************************************************\n * Copyright (C) 2010 Tadeus Prastowo (eus@member.fsf.org)                   *\n *                                                                           *\n * This program is free software